# POSIX requires `{` to be a complete, delimited reserved WORD to open a brace
# group. `{a` glues the brace to the word, so `{a; }` is NOT a brace group — the
# delimited `LBrace` token refuses to match `{` as a prefix of `{a`, and the input
# is a syntax error (`{a` is an ordinary command word with no following command).
<<<cmd
printf '{a; }\n' | "$PP" run std.shell --input -
<<<assert
exit-not 0
